<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $41.7 mln May 5.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $41.7 mln May 5.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $41.7 million surplus on May 5 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 5</p>
<p>Exports: $258.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $256.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $304.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $264.7 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $41.7 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $408.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $426 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $489.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $423.8 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $48.1 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
